From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm glue: TF_GLM_OVN_HC_ROWS=16|32 and TF_GLM_OVN_HC_DEC, hc mixing with fewer weight reads

Ported from ai-engine fork-ssh/ovn-up's 6c92d7ec2 (2026-10-30). The mixing
pass reads each block's weights once a 4-row step and once a 16-block row; the
fork's variants stage 16 or 32 prompt rows a block (HC_ROWS) and run the
hc.cu decode layout for windows under 64 rows (HC_DEC, 16 x 3 x rows/4, 288
threads), every row on today's chain so the bytes are unchanged.

Adapted by hand, not replayed: this series has no ROUTER16 field or loader at
the site the fork's patch hooks, so the two optional-kernel groups are loaded
by hcLoad() from Kernels.loadOvn instead; the launches go through
cuda_pdl.launch, which applies TF_GLM_PDL itself, so the fork's explicit .pdl
flags and cuda.launch.launch calls are gone; and the build step is attached to
test-glm-keep-seqs-host, which exists here. The fork's GPU reference check
(glm_ref_hc_rows / glm_ref_ovn) is not carried: it needs the forked
glm_ref_tests registry this series does not have. cuda_hc_ovn_test.zig is
carried as the host receipt of the choice, grid and arguments; glm_hc_bench.zig
is not carried and the measurement is the arm below.

Receipts here: the host test's launch records (16/32-row grids, HC_DEC's
288-thread launch, the knobs-off paths), and the two rows' parsing.
Measurement: a fresh arm on the current series, HC_DEC=1 against unset at 1, 2,
4, 6 and 8 streams with replies equal (the fork read +1.0% at P8 and +0.4% at
P4, before the re-seat), and HC_ROWS=16|32 on cold 8k / 32k / 120k.

